org/wikipedia/commons/1/14/Norderney%2C_D%C3%BCnenlandschaft%2C_Wegweiser_--_2025_--_9437.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Norderney,_D%C3%BCnenlandschaft,_Wegweiser_--_2025_--_9437.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=174516222","extmetadata":{"ObjectName":{"value":"Norderney, Dünenlandschaft, Wegweiser -- 2025 -- 9437","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Dune landscape with signpost to the wreck at the eastern end in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Saxony\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Lower Saxony\">Lower Saxon</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wadden_Sea\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Wadden Sea\">Wadden Sea</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:National park\">National Park</a> (quiet zone), <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norderney\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Norderney\">Norderney</a>, Lower Saxony, Germany<br><small>The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Saxon_Wadden_Sea_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Lower Saxon Wadden Sea National Park\">Lower Saxon Wadden Sea National Park</a> was established in 1986 and encompasses the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Frisian_Islands\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:East Frisian Islands\">East Frisian Islands</a>, mudflats, and sea <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidal_marsh\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Tidal marsh\">marshes</a> between Dollart on the border with the Netherlands in the west and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuxhaven\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Cuxhaven\">Cuxhaven</a> to the Outer <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbe\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Elbe\">Elbe</a> shipping channel in the east. The Lower Saxon Wadden Sea National Park, together with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schleswig-Holstein_Wadden_Sea_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Schleswig-Holstein Wadden Sea National Park\">Schleswig-Holstein Wadden Sea National Park</a>, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg_Wadden_Sea_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Hamburg Wadden Sea National Park\">Hamburg Wadden Sea National Park</a>, the Danish <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wadden_Sea_National_Park,_Denmark\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Wadden Sea National Park, Denmark\">Vadehavet National Park</a>, and the Dutch Wadden Sea, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. In addition, the national park was recognized as a biosphere reserve in 1992 under the UNESCO “Man and Biosphere” program, has been a registered <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_Area_of_Conservation\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Special Area of Conservation\">Fauna-Flora Habitat</a> area under the European FFH Directive since 1997 with zones I and II, and has also been a registered bird sanctuary under the European Birds Directive since 2000. The national park is therefore part of the Natura 2000 network and protection regime.</small>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q34788025\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q34788025\"><span title=\"German photographer and mathematician\">Dietmar Rabich</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},{"pageid":191275011,"ns":6,"title":"File:Common yellow gilder (Cymothoe egesta egesta) underside 2.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":6595913,"width":3537,"height":3401,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e5/Common_yellow_glider_%28Cymothoe_egesta_egesta%29_underside_2.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":3840,"thumbheight":3692,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia